sion  of what happened from the  previous versions you've heard and then  there's this hole in it which gets  filled  in the fourth book so i hope by the time  it's all finished  i will have expanded backwards as well  as gone forwards  and many of the many of the gaps will  have been filled in and you'll know more  about the whole robert and  rhaegar and everything like that  but it's not quite the same as telling a  story about them i realized  he also said he did not think it would  make sense for hbo to make a show based  on robert's rebellion because once all  of his books are finished  we will already know everything about  that moment in history  with that being said it seems as if he  changed his mind  if everything in the article is accurate  it seems like entertainment weekly does  have a great relationship with hbo  because they're always getting the  exclusives  so as of right now i will go with what  it says  hopefully hbo officially releases more  details soon  let me show you what it says because  this is very interesting as well  hbo wants to order more game of thrones  successor shows  in addition to the upcoming prequel  series house of the dragon  the network is looking to potentially  greenlight more shows said in the world  of westeros sources say one of which  just reported by variety is a project  based on dunkin egg and early  development  the dunkin egg stories by author george  r martin follow the adventures of sir  duncan the tall  and a young aegon targaryen v  they are set 90 years before the events  in game of thrones  now all of you should already know i  would absolutely love this because it  would most likely mean we would get more  blood raven as well  that's not all hbo has been meeting with  several top writers and throwing out  other ideas based on martin's works  among the ideas being contemplated is a  series based on robert's rebellion  which was the war for the iron throne  that upended westeros a couple of  decades before the events in game of  thrones  one of the writers is a name familiar to  the hbo genre fans  bruno heller who created the acclaimed  historical drama rome  a series that was seen as a bit of a  short-lived precursor to thrones that  said  no writer has yet officially signed on  to any of the series in development  there are no sequels or spin-offs from  the original series currently under  consideration  the idea is for hbo to go big on thrones  for hbo and hbo max in a way  that's not entirely unlike what disney  has done to star wars  disney announced 10 star wars shows  during its investor day conference in  december  and the next day the company's stock  shot up 14  to an all-time high while after thrones  ended in 2019  hbo saw its linear adult demo viewership  drop as it struggled to fill the dragon  size hole in its lineup  hbo's parent company warner media is  investing heavily in hbo max in general  they see the streaming service as it's  you win or you die effort to future  proof the company's entertainment  division  the new move is also similar to hbo's  then unprecedented bake off of making  five different thrones prequel projects  into the development before the series  ended  an operation that ultimately resulted in  one episode being shot that did not move  forward  that was of course the series about the  long night  and another house of the dragon by  co-showrunners ryan condell and miguel  sapochnick  being green led to series this new surge  in development is arguably more intense  however  as it's not just looking for a single  successor but  ideally more than one worthy title to  join house of the dragon on the air  wow like i said before i was not  expecting this  now like most shows that are in the  works they may never see the light of  day  just because they're working on these  does not mean they will get a full  series order like house of the dragon  did  either way they must have done something  to sweeten the deal to get george r  martin to change his mind  now most of you should already know i  would absolutely love to see robert's  rebellion  i think a lot of fans want to see this  series get made  i think it might even have the best  chance of success considering it would  look  and feel so much like the original game  of thrones  now i guess you could also say that is a  double-edged sword there are  also a lot of fans who would hate this  because it would remind them of game of  thrones so much  it could end up just being a reminder of  what happens at the end of season 8.  since we all know that's where the story  is heading anyway i don't agree with  that however just because game of  thrones ended the way it did does not  affect the way i look at future shows  now that dan and dave aren't there i  would like to think things will be done  differently  but none of us will know for sure until  we see the new episodes  the fact that hbo is getting this  aggressive about making more shows set  in this universe has me very excited  i've said it before and i will say it  again i will watch any show adapted from  this amazing world  george rr martin has created i will be  keeping my eyes open from here on out  i want to see if hbo confirms the news  but what i really want to see is if  george rr martin confirms the news  he's the one who said they would not  make anything based on duncan egg or  robert's rebellion  for now i will remain excited as always  make sure you subscribe so you can stay  up to date on any and all information  regarding game of thrones  house of the dragon or any other shows  hbo wants to make  like i said in my last video i will also  let you know whenever i find out any new  information  let me know what you think about these  new developments down below  which of these shows do you want to see  the most as always i want to thank you  all for watching the video  i will see you again very soon bye  [Music]  [Music]  you

